# Generated film assets — frames, VO stems, test renders. 540MB and growing;
# output/ was already ignored, these were the gap.
#
# Note the shape: `videos/**` not `videos/`. Git will not descend into an
# excluded DIRECTORY, so a trailing-slash exclude makes the `!` re-includes
# below dead letters. Excluding the contents instead, then re-including the
# subdirectories, keeps the scripts and cut lists tracked — SCRIPT.md carries
# the verified citations and generate.mjs carries the frame prompts.
videos/**
!videos/*/
!videos/*/*.md
!videos/*/*.mjs
# .py and .json carry work that cannot be reconstructed: the edit decision list
# (edl-*.json — the actual cut), the content-lock/re-time pass (place-*.py), the
# narration segment timings (segments.json), and the fal.ai job audit trail.
# All small text. Losing them means redoing a placement pass, not a re-download.
!videos/*/*.py
!videos/*/*.json
# The locked script is the file everything else derives from - narration,
# captions, the board's 1:1 sentence mapping. It is the least reconstructible
# text in the tree.
!videos/*/*.txt
# One level deeper for delivery kits — the .md there is the publish copy.
# Media in deliver/ stays ignored by the videos/** rule above.
!videos/*/*/
!videos/*/*/*.md
tmp/
vendor/agent-reach/

# compiled python is an artifact, never source
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# packages/provenance/ is a pointer to github.com/isaacsight/provenance-substrate (moved out 2026-08-17)
!packages/provenance/
!packages/provenance/README.md
